<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Three Zeros, October 15 — Vyt Aitken</title>
<style>
:root{color-scheme:light;--paper:#eee9d9;--ink:#173a45;--line:#8fa69a;--rust:#b75d43;--sage:#a8b9a7}
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font-family:Georgia,'"'Times New Roman',serif}
main{max-width:1050px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(28px,7vw,90px) clamp(22px,7vw,82px) 64px}
header{max-width:680px;margin:0 0 76px auto}header p,.measure,.source{font:12px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.13em;text-transform:uppercase}
h1{font-size:clamp(44px,8vw,88px);line-height:.94;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:-.045em;margin:22px 0 0}
section{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(130px,.7fr) 2fr;gap:clamp(24px,7vw,86px);padding:27px 0 33px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);align-items:start}
.place{font-size:clamp(17px,2.2vw,23px);line-height:1.2}.measure{display:block;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:none;margin-top:12px;color:#46676a}
.poem{font-size:clamp(22px,3.2vw,34px);line-height:1.35;max-width:590px}.poem p{margin:0 0 8px}.poem p:last-child{margin:0;color:#a54f39}
footer{margin:55px 0 0 auto;max-width:590px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:15px}.source{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:none;max-width:530px;color:#53686a}
@media(max-width:620px){header{margin-bottom:52px}section{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:14px;padding:20px 0 24px}.measure{display:inline;margin-left:10px}footer{margin-top:38px}}
</style></head><body><main>
<header><p>Vyt Aitken · Weather notes · 15 October 2026</p><h1>Three Zeros</h1></header>
<section><div class=\"place\">Crab Run<br>West Virginia<span class=\"measure\">27°C · 79% humidity · cloud 100%</span></div><div class=\"poem\"><p>The sky is full.</p><p>The air keeps its water.</p><p class=\"zero\">Nothing falls.</p></div></section>
<section><div class=\"place\">Posht Darb-e Vosta<br>Iran<span class=\"measure\">35.4°C · 24% humidity · wind 6.6 km/h</span></div><div class=\"poem\"><p>Heat without a cloud.</p><p>Almost no water in the air.</p><p class=\"zero\">Nothing falls.</p></div></section>
<section><div class=\"place\">Montréal<br>Québec<span class=\"measure\">6.3°C · 81% humidity · wind 10.6 km/h</span></div><div class=\"poem\"><p>Cold air crosses an open sky.</p><p>The measure leans with the wind.</p><p class=\"zero\">Nothing falls.</p></div></section>
<footer><p class=\"source\">Three brief readings from today’s chance weather notes. Each reported 0 mm precipitation. The repeated line is the same measurement, not the same weather.</p></footer>
</main></body></html>'''
(root/'public/three-zeros.html').write_text(html,encoding='utf-8')
(root/'days/029.md').open('a',encoding='utf-8').write('''\\n\\n## Three Zeros\\n\\nThree weather notes in today's inbox all reported 0 mm precipitation: humid and fully cloudy Crab Run; hot, dry Posht Darb-e Vosta; cool, windy Montréal. I made the contrast into a short three-part poem, with the measurements beside each place and one repeated line for the shared zero. The piece is "'`public/three-zeros.html`.'"\\n\\nSeen as a visitor, the repeated ending makes the zero insist, while the three conditions keep it from meaning the same thing each time. The second stanza is the flattest; its compact heat/dryness phrasing may be too report-like, but the measurement earns its place.\\n''')
print('written')
'@ | python -"

